 420 60 361 29 314C21 301 19 297 19 294C19 285 25 284 38 284C55 284 54 284 61 295C70 308 90 328 103 336C134 358 146 358 196 358L228 358L220 334C195 249 161 166 111 61L98 33L98 22C98 13 98 11 100 6C106-5 119-11 132-11C150-11 168 1 175 17C193 47 268 350 268 354L269 358L367 358C367 357 365 348 362 336C345 266 336 217 331 169C330 157 330 139 330 121C330 73 336 40 349 10C356-4 360-10 381-10C410-10 431 15 431 37Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2023 JEE Main 2023 (Online) 15th April Morning Shift Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 15th April Morning Shift","nextq":"lgnzrkr2","prevq":"lgnz9975","questions":[{"question_id":"lgnzeywd","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2023-online-15th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 15th April Morning Shift","permalink":"which-of-the-following-statement-is-correct-for-paper-chroma-jee-main-chemistry-aph1uwbwrsqlwpcz","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"Which of the following statement is correct for paper chromatography?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Water present in the mobile phase gets absorbed by the paper which then forms the stationary phase."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Water present in the pores of the paper forms the stationary phase."},{"identifier":"C","content":" Paper sheet forms the stationary phase."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Paper and water present in its pores together form the stationary phase."}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"The correct statement for paper chromatography is:\n<br/><br/>\n(B) Water present in the pores of the paper forms the stationary phase.\n<br/><br/>\nIn paper chromatography, the stationary phase is the water that is absorbed and trapped in the pores of the paper, while the mobile phase is a liquid solvent that moves through the paper carrying the sample with it. The different components of the sample have different affinities for the stationary phase and the mobile phase, causing them to move at different rates and separate from each other on the paper."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>पेपर क्रोमेटोग्रैफी (कागज़ वर्णलेखन) के संदर्भ में निम्न में से कौन सा कथन सत्य है?</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"गतिशील प्रावस्था में उपस्थित जल को पेपर द्वारा अवशोषित किया जाता है, जो अब स्थिर प्रावस्था"},{"identifier":"B","content":"पेपर के छिद्रों में उपस्थित जल स्थिर प्रावस्था का कार्य करता है।"},{"identifier":"C","content":"पेपर शीट स्थिर प्रावस्था का कार्य करता है।"},{"identifier":"D","content":"पेपर  एवं उसके छिद्रों में उपस्थित जल स्थिर प्रावस्था का कार्य करता है।"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"पेपर क्रोमैटोग्राफी (कागज़ वर्णलेखन) के लिए सही कथन है:\n<br/><br/>\n(B) कागज़ के छिद्रों में उपस्थित जल स्थिर प्रावस्था बनाता है।\n<br/><br/>\nपेपर क्रोमैटोग्राफी में, स्थिर प्रावस्था वह जल होता है जो कागज़ के छिद्रों में अवशोषित और आबद्ध (trapped) होता है, जबकि गतिशील प्रावस्था एक द्रव विलायक होती है जो नमूने को अपने साथ ले जाते हुए कागज़ के माध्यम से गति करती है। नमूने के विभिन्न घटकों की स्थिर प्रावस्था और गतिशील प्रावस्था के प्रति अलग-अलग बंधुता होती है, जिसके कारण वे अलग-अलग दरों पर गति करते हैं और कागज़ पर एक-दूसरे से पृथक हो जाते हैं।"}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"purification-of-organic-compounds","type":"mcq","year":2023,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2023-online-15th-april-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"lgnzgm5p","chapter":"biomolecules","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2023-online-15th-april-morning-shift","paperTitl