ng Shift Chemistry - Biomolecules Question 72 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgrkncln/e55d2b89-9ff2-4a0a-82e1-ca339d60d119/fd7b65b0-e0d2-11ed-8b13-b3bb227d6f90/file-1lgrknclo.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgrkncln/e55d2b89-9ff2-4a0a-82e1-ca339d60d119/fd7b65b0-e0d2-11ed-8b13-b3bb227d6f90/file-1lgrknclo.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgrkncln/e55d2b89-9ff2-4a0a-82e1-ca339d60d119/fd7b65b0-e0d2-11ed-8b13-b3bb227d6f90/file-1lgrknclo.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lgrkncln/e55d2b89-9ff2-4a0a-82e1-ca339d60d119/fd7b65b0-e0d2-11ed-8b13-b3bb227d6f90/file-1lgrknclo.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lgrkncln/e55d2b89-9ff2-4a0a-82e1-ca339d60d119/fd7b65b0-e0d2-11ed-8b13-b3bb227d6f90/file-1lgrknclo.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lgrkncln/e55d2b89-9ff2-4a0a-82e1-ca339d60d119/fd7b65b0-e0d2-11ed-8b13-b3bb227d6f90/file-1lgrknclo.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"><br>Arginine is an amino acid that has a basic side chain containing a guanidino group. The other three options are true for arginine:\n<br><br>\n(A) It has a fairly high melting point due to the presence of strong ionic interactions between the positively charged guanidino group and the negatively charged carboxylate group in the solid state.<br><br>\n(B) It is associated with more than one pKa values because it contains multiple ionizable groups, including the amino group, the carboxylate group, and the guanidino group. These groups can dissociate in a stepwise manner, leading to multiple pKa values.<br><br>\n(D) It is a crystalline solid due to the presence of strong ionic interactions between the positively charged guanidino group and the negatively charged carboxylate group, which leads to the formation of a well-ordered crystal lattice.\n<br><br>\nHowever, option (C) is not true because arginine is not soluble in benzene. This is because benzene is a nonpolar solvent, and arginine is a polar and charged molecule. Therefore, arginine is more soluble in polar solvents such as water and less soluble in nonpolar solvents such as benzene."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>आर्जिनीन के लिए कौन सही नहीं हैं?</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"इसका गलनांक उच्च है।"},{"identifier":"B","content":"इसके पास एक से अधिक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.537ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.006ex\" height=\"2.082ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1770.6 920.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use><use data-c=\"4B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4B\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1367,-229.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> मान है।"},{"identifier":"C","content":"बेन्जीन में इसकी विलेयता उच्च है।"},{"identifier":"D","content":"यह एक क्रिस्टलीय ठोस है।"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"vitamins-and-nucleic-acids","type":"mcq","year":2023,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2023-online-15th-april-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"lgnzj56q","chapter":"compounds-containing-nitrogen","chapterGroup":"organ